The folding using C++ will probably work. I'm just not that proficient with javascript and till didn't fully grok the ACE modes.

I'm sure the templates could be added, but I'm not sure how without digging through the code. Everything in rstudio is basically hard-coded into the IDE. There's no sort of overall plugin interface for new languages. So, I had to poke around the source until I found where things were defined, change stuff and see whether it did what I hoped it would do. And repeat.

Also, I figured that the most minimal change in the source would be the most likely to be accepted by rstudio if I ever did submit a pull request. From the rstudio source, it looks like it has language modes for python, SQL, javascript, and yaml. So, I thought that adding syntax support when loading a "*.stan" file would be fine, but making changes to the main menu may be too much.  But really, it was just a huge pita to figure out their code.

